Find and Inspect Container Images
Objectives
Find containerized applications in container registries and get information about the runtime parameters of supported and community container images.

1. Container Image Overview
Container
A container is an isolated runtime environment where an application runs.
Features:
•	Runs as an isolated process
•	Uses Linux namespaces
•	Does not interfere with host or other containers
Container Image
A container image is a packaged application that contains:
•	application code
•	libraries
•	dependencies
•	runtime environment
Important:
•	Image = blueprint
•	Container = running instance
Example:
Container Image → used to create → Container
You can run many containers from one image.
Example:
nginx image
   ├── container 1
   ├── container 2
   └── container 3
