6. Container Image Identifier
A container image has four main identifiers.
Example image:
registry.access.redhat.com/ubi10/httpd-24:1
1 Registry
registry.access.redhat.com
Image server.
________________________________________
2 Repository Name
ubi10/httpd-24
Location of image inside registry.
________________________________________
3 Tag
:1
Version of image.
Example:
nginx:1.24
nginx:latest
If tag not specified:
latest
is used.
________________________________________
4 Image ID / Hash
Example:
sha256:4186a1ead13fc307...
Important properties:
•	unique identifier
•	cannot change
•	ensures image integrity
________________________________________
7. Container Image Components
Container images contain layers + metadata.
________________________________________
Layers
Each instruction in a container build creates a layer.
Example build:
FROM ubi
RUN install apache
COPY website files
Layers stack like:
Layer 3 → app files
Layer 2 → apache
Layer 1 → base OS
Advantages:
•	faster downloads
•	reuse layers
•	smaller updates
________________________________________
Metadata
Metadata stores configuration and instructions.
Example:
•	environment variables
•	commands
•	exposed ports
•	working directory
________________________________________
8. Container Image Instructions
Some instructions affect container execution.
________________________________________
ENV
Defines environment variables.
Example:
ENV DB_HOST=mysql
________________________________________
ARG
Build-time variables.
Used during image build.
________________________________________
USER
Defines container user.
Example:
USER 1001
Security best practice → avoid root user.
In OpenShift:
•	regular users run containers as random UID
________________________________________
ENTRYPOINT
Defines executable program.
Example:
ENTRYPOINT ["python"]
________________________________________
CMD
Default command executed.
Example:
CMD ["app.py"]
Final execution:
python app.py
________________________________________
WORKDIR
Working directory inside container.
Example:
WORKDIR /app
________________________________________
9. Metadata Instructions (Documentation Only)
These do not affect runtime behavior.
________________________________________
EXPOSE
Documents which port the app uses.
Example:
EXPOSE 8080
Does NOT automatically expose the port.
________________________________________
VOLUME
Defines persistent storage.
Example:
VOLUME /data
________________________________________
LABEL
Metadata key-value.
Example:
LABEL maintainer="admin@example.com"
________________________________________
