13. Inspecting Images with Skopeo
Skopeo is a tool to inspect container images without pulling them.
Features:
•	inspect images
•	copy images
•	delete images
•	sync registries
Install:
sudo dnf install skopeo
________________________________________
14. Login to Registry
Example:
skopeo login quay.io
Credentials stored in:
$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/containers/auth.json
________________________________________
15. List Image Tags
Command:
skopeo list-tags docker://registry.access.redhat.com/ubi10/httpd-24
Output:
Tags:
1
latest
10.0
________________________________________
16. Inspect Container Image
Command:
skopeo inspect docker://registry.access.redhat.com/ubi10/httpd-24
Shows:
•	environment variables
•	ports
•	commands
•	image layers
•	architecture
Example output info:
User: 1001
Entrypoint: container-entrypoint
Cmd: /usr/bin/run-httpd
Ports: 8080, 8443
________________________________________
17. Copy Container Image
Command:
skopeo copy docker://quay.io/skopeo/stable:latest \
docker://registry.example.com/skopeo:latest
Copies image between registries.
________________________________________
18. Delete Container Image
Command:
skopeo delete docker://registry.example.com/skopeo:latest
Removes image from registry.
________________________________________
19. Sync Container Images
Command:
skopeo sync --src docker --dest docker \
registry.access.redhat.com/ubi10/httpd-24 registry.example.com/httpd-24
Synchronizes images between registries.
________________________________________
20. Inspect Images Using OpenShift
OpenShift CLI command:
oc image info IMAGE
Example:
oc image info registry.access.redhat.com/ubi10/httpd-24
Shows:
•	image ID
•	layers
•	architecture
•	commands
•	environment variables
Example:
Digest: sha256:b765...
________________________________________
