22. Why Containers Should Not Run as Root
Running containers as root is dangerous.
Risk:
1.	attacker exploits container
2.	escapes container
3.	gains root access to host
OpenShift solves this by:
random UID assignment
for containers.
________________________________________
23. Limitations of Non-root Containers
Some limitations exist:
•	cannot bind to ports below 1024
•	cannot use ping
•	cannot run privileged utilities
Solution:
•	use port forwarding
•	use non-root compatible images
